# Every exposure that had nowhere to go. One row per layer where every buffer is accounted for and
# none of them has room, beside the exposure its own two measurements imply.
#
# The argument is the whole row
#   The argument is the whole row and never one column. Read as "the capacity buffer is a stated
#   zero", this is one route closed rather than nowhere to go: the same layer could still have
#   drawn on stock or made the demand wait. Two rules rest on this population, and from that
#   premise both conclude that somebody went without, which does not carry it. `S` is an L x 3
#   matrix and the three buffers are substitutes; the index belongs in a column, which is where
#   assets/ddl/schema.ddl has always kept it.
#
# The escape clause holds for all three buffers
#   The escape clause that makes it sound is written for one buffer and true of three. "An absent
#   capacity slack licenses none of this, because nobody knows whether the supply could have
#   stretched." The same holds of inventory and of time, and a clause carried to one of three
#   reads as though the other two were settled.
#
# It rests on `stated`, not on `measured`
#   Every zero carries a `boundOrigin`, so the population can be read back, and none of the
#   capacity zeros was measured: `contractual`, a reserved block somebody negotiated, and
#   `intrinsic`, a material limit. A shelf life entails a zero, a negotiation fixes one, an
#   observation records one, and all three are somebody saying the buffer is empty and standing
#   behind it.
#
# Two rules, two questions
#   Two rules read this relation and they ask different questions of it. One wants the layers with
#   no named holder; the other wants every one of them, against the shares that were admitted.
#   Inlined at both call sites, these joins are two copies of one population, which is one edit
#   away from two populations under one argument.
-- layers/exposure_scope.sqlc, restricted to the standing that licenses a conclusion.
SELECT s.*
FROM (
    :compose(layers/exposure_scope.sqlc)
) s
WHERE s.standing = 'every buffer sized and empty'
